A||||6||Fiero*101||Thermostat cap problem||||1||
Z||000000||Fiero*101||09-17-2001||06:14 PM||||My thermostat cap WILL NOT STOP LEAKING antifreeze!<BR>I just got a new cap b/c I thought that was the problem but it wasnt its coming from the top and botom of the cap.<P>PLEASE HELP!<P>Fiero*101||||reg||1
Z||000001||johnt671||09-17-2001||06:46 PM||||Make sure your thermostat is all the way down, and look real close at the neck of the thermostat housing for splits and cracks.  Could be the plastic has gotten weak. and is making it look like the cap is leaking.  Also check the gasket on the cap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-17-2001||06:52 PM||||the housing may also be rough/worn or you don't have the cap on all the way. It can be tought to tighten it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||09-17-2001||10:28 PM||||Hey 101!<BR>I had a problem with my cap leaking, turned out to be the thermostat housing...<BR>Seems the lip of the housing had rusted underneath, and weakened it...<BR>I replaced it, and no more leaks...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dragon||09-17-2001||10:53 PM||||What brand cap are you using.  I have gotten to the point that I prefer GM||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||09-18-2001||12:27 AM||||Also, make sure you're getting the cap on all the way. The arrows should line up with the hoses.  I can't tighten mine by hand, I have to use a pair of Channel Lok's to get it fully tight, but no leaks.  [fingers crossed]<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><I><FONT COLOR="blue">The path of the righteous man is beset on all sides by the inequities of the selfish and the tyrranys of evil men. Blessed is he who in the name of charity and good will shepards the weak through the valley of darkness for he is truly his brothers keeper, and the finder of lost children. And I shall strike down upon thee with great vengence and furious anger, those who attempt to poison and destroy my brothers. And you will know my name is the lord when I lay my vengence upon thee. </I></FONT></FONT><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/9-11-01a.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierohoho||09-18-2001||02:50 AM||||I had a similar problem with mine.<P>I took a small file,(not a rasp) and ran it lightly over the top, I had it resting flat across the seal area, I cleaned the scale/rust/crud off that way.<P>I saw a post when I first came on the forum and someone was using a small oil filter wrench to put on or remove the cap, I tried this and it worked great, Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
